  "term": "method of equal-appearing intervals",
  "definition": "A psychophysical method for studying larger perceived differences by arranging three stimuli so that the gap from the first to the second seems equal to the gap from the second to the third. It compares stimulus changes that look equally large, rather than changes that are merely just noticeable.",
